# Supabase — copy to `.env.local` (never commit `.env.local`).
#
# PROJECT URL (not on the API Keys tab):
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → General → Project URL
#   Looks like: https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
#
# PUBLIC KEY FOR NEXT.JS BROWSER CODE:
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys → tab "Publishable and secret API keys"
#   Copy the Publishable key (starts with sb_publishable_...) under "Publishable key".
#   Put it below as NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — same role as the old "anon" JWT:
#   safe for the client when Row Level Security (RLS) is enforced.
#
# LEGACY KEYS (only if a tutorial asks for "anon"):
#   Same page → tab "Legacy anon, service_role API keys" → copy "anon" public.
#
# NEVER expose "Secret" / service_role keys in NEXT_PUBLIC_* or frontend code.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here
